    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Medical oncology (gastrointestinal) consultation within two weeks, with colorectal surgery, to review the colonoscopy and any biopsy with her and plan staging and treatment if cancer is found. Guideline: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Rectal Cancer (current version); summarized in Benson AB, et al. NCCN Guidelines Insights: Rectal Cancer, Version 3.2024. J Natl Compr Canc Netw 2024;22(6):366-375 (PMID 39151454) (2026); Scott AJ, et al. Management of Locally Advanced Rectal Cancer: ASCO Guideline. J Clin Oncol 2024;42(28):3355-3375 (PMID 39116386) (2024) [S]</item><item>Urgent work-up of rectal bleeding with a change in bowel habit and a rectal mass in a woman under 50: colonoscopy with biopsy within days, with mismatch repair testing of any cancer; blood count, ferritin, chemistry and CEA; if cancer is confirmed, rectal-protocol MRI of the pelvis and CT of the chest, abdomen and pelvis; return at once for heavy bleeding, fainting or inability to pass stool. Guideline: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Rectal Cancer (current version); summarized in Benson AB, et al. NCCN Guidelines Insights: Rectal Cancer, Version 3.2024. J Natl Compr Canc Netw 2024;22(6):366-375 (PMID 39151454) (2026); Colorectal Cancer: Screening (JAMA 2021;325(19):1965-1977, PMID 34003218) (2021) [S]</item><item>Distress and depression screening at each visit; plain explanations with written information; attention to sexual health and body image and to her golf, with an exercise plan she sets; she decides who is told and who receives each note. Guideline: Ligibel JA, et al. Exercise, Diet, and Weight Management During Cancer Treatment: ASCO Guideline. J Clin Oncol 2022;40(22):2491-2507 (PMID 35576506) (2022); Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023) [S]</item></list></text>

